@page "/change-password-required"
@layout OnboardingLayout
@attribute [Authorize]
@using Odyssey.Client.Components

<PageTitle>Choose a new password</PageTitle>

@*
    ChangePasswordRequired — the forced password-change gate (issue #406 §3, design system
    ChangePasswordRequired.jsx).

    Where a user lands when MustChangePassword is set on their account. Two causes reach it: an admin
    triggered "Send password reset" on /users (#406), or the account is the bootstrap administrator the
    migrations job seeded from configuration, whose password is a one-time secret (#290). Rendered under
    the nav-less OnboardingLayout — no rail, no command palette, no way into the app — because a forced
    credential change outranks everything else, including the legal and profile onboarding gates.

    This page is presentation only. The block is the API's: while the flag is set every endpoint except
    five answers 403, so deleting this page (or driving the API with a stolen cookie) changes nothing
    about what the account can do. What it buys is that the user meets a form instead of a wall of
    failed requests.

    A user who does NOT know their current password can leave: Sign out and the Forgot password link are
    both present and keyboard-reachable without passing through the password fields.
*@

<div class="onb-shell">
    <div class="onb-card cpr-card">
        <div class="onb-brand">
            <OdsBrandMark Size="68" />
        </div>

        <div class="onb-head">
            @* tabindex="-1" so focus can move here once after the first render: the user arrives by an
               involuntary redirect, so the reason has to be announced rather than left silent. *@
            <h1 @ref="_headingRef" tabindex="-1" class="onb-title">Choose a new password</h1>
            @* Wording true of BOTH causes, not just the admin-reset one: a bootstrap administrator
               (issue #290) is seeded with a one-time password nobody "asked" them to change. The flag
               carries no reason, and a second column plus branching copy would be disproportionate to
               one sentence. Keep id="cpr-explanation" — OdsPasswordChangeForm's DescribedBy points at
               it, so renaming it silently drops the first field's accessible description. *@
            <p class="onb-sub" id="cpr-explanation">
                You must choose a new password before continuing.
            </p>
        </div>

        @* DescribedBy, not a wrapping div carrying aria-describedby: the attribute only applies to the
           element it sits on, so a role-less wrapper would associate the explanation with nothing. The
           component puts it on the first field instead, where a user landing straight in the form hears
           it. *@
        <OdsPasswordChangeForm @ref="_form"
                               OnSubmit="SubmitAsync"
                               Error="@_error"
                               Busy="_saving"
                               Columns="2"
                               AutoFocus="true"
                               DescribedBy="cpr-explanation"
                               SubmitLabel="Set new password"
                               BusyLabel="Setting…" />

        <div class="cpr-alt">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Outlined.HelpOutline" Size="Size.Small" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span>
                Don’t know your current password?
                <MudLink Href="/forgot-password">Use Forgot password</MudLink> instead.
            </span>
        </div>

        <div class="onb-actions cpr-actions">
            <MudButton Variant="Variant.Text"
                       StartIcon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Logout"
                       Disabled="_saving"
                       OnClick="SignOutAsync">Sign out</MudButton>
        </div>

        <div class="onb-foot">
            <MudIcon Icon="@Icons.Material.Filled.Lock" Size="Size.Small" aria-hidden="true" />
            <span>
                You’ve been signed out of your other devices. Your current password keeps working until
                you set a new one.
            </span>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
